cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this archive, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Reproducibility archive for dataset provenance, sample overlap and direction preservation in cross-cohort reproducibility of transcriptomic biomarker claims: an empirical methodological study in psoriasis"
abstract: >-
  This repository contains processed analysis inputs, claim-level eligibility decisions,
  cross-accession sample-overlap exclusions, reproducible analysis code, numerical outputs,
  sensitivity analyses, paired audit-impact analyses, and publication figures supporting an
  empirical methodological study of transcriptomic biomarker reproducibility in psoriasis.
  The final source-adjudicated development analysis contains 33 paper-gene claims representing
  32 genes and 176 eligible cohort contributions. The archive also contains a separate small
  RNA-seq boundary cohort and complete provenance and audit materials.
